{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And I will see the blood and I will pass over you.</b> It is not the blood that prevents the plague, nor does its absence bring the plague; rather, Scripture teaches you that whoever believed in the Holy One, blessed be He, with complete faith, and suspended his trust upon Him, and did not worry about the terror of Pharaoh and his decree, and slaughtered in public the abomination of Egypt, and put of the blood of the Paschal offering upon the doorposts and upon the lintel — behold, this one is righteous and trusted in the Holy One, blessed be He; he is worthy that He should shield him from the plague and the destroyer." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'And I will see the blood' — but is it not written (Daniel 2:22), ״He knows what is in the darkness״, and it is written (Psalms 139:12), ״Even darkness does not darken from You״? What does Scripture mean by 'And I will see the blood'? Rather: I see the blood of the binding of Isaac your father, as it is said (Genesis 22:14), ״And he called the name of that place YHWH Yireh.״"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:05.037643756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}